From 32ce16e7be6761e4aeaeb44aed551c1727ccbc88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 10:28:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] E-Ink: outline shared surfaces and remove tonal elevation

Change-Id: Ia16b31c2e145fdc387f94246d55fe7cb1500794f

Give the quick-settings outline layer an id so later code can replace it by id.

SettingsCard.kt and SettingsTheme.kt keep the upstream formatting; only the outline, surface colour and tonal-elevation lines change (no formatter-only hunks).

Inactive slider tracks use one light grey (#BDBDBD): the SettingsLib expressive slider (Sound volume and other SliderPreferences) and the SPA slider (was near-black). EinkSurfaces (PlatformComposeCore) gives SystemUI Compose the flat check, the whole-pixel edge width, the edge and the track grey.

Compose edges (SPA has no window border for Compose dialogs and popups): alert dialogs, dialog cards and content, overflow/copy/dropdown/spinner menus, grouped lists (one edge per group), main switch, action icon buttons, spinner buttons, suggestion card, card count and banner. SPA spinner options and the profile tab show selection by inversion. View SettingsLib edges: main switch bar (expressive and on/off), tonal buttons, expressive banner card, CardPreference; highlighted rows get a double-width edge on white instead of a translucent tone. SystemUI Compose bottom sheets (volume panel, shortcut helper) get an edge.

Notification footer buttons keep an outline (no colour filter when flat); long-press guts carry the row outline at the notification radius; screenshot and clipboard preview frame and action chip container are outlined.

Dropped the View QS tile outline layers (dead with the Compose QS fragment).

Carries the SettingsLib v36 surface colours and theme backgrounds formerly in frameworks_base/0001 (moved unchanged).
